<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept pepper exports fall.</title>
<headline>Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept pepper exports fall.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's exports of black pepper fell 38.2 percent to $32 million in the first nine months of 1996 from $51.8 million in the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Exports amounted to $19.7 million in the same 1994 period.</p>
<p>The finance ministry released the data ahead of President Suharto's unveiling of the 1997/98 (April-March) state budget in parliament on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
